# Inert803 policy-only phase budget adoption

Source-only adoption inside the existing INERT PolicyCellBudget, not production routes, template-owner adapter, Finance or PMO readers. Frozen39563290 metadata primitive and6e0d2aa codec files remain unchanged. New policy_budget_v2 includes only four policy cell specs; global1MiB/100cells and policy-local1MiB/100cells are marker-owned across wrappers, with conservative independent charges to ALL exact server entry output domains. This is not precise per-domain provenance and not yet cross-Finance/PMO accounting.

Actor is required at budget construction, bound to the fresh server snapshot principal object+PK, entry keyset, default connection and rawconnection. One-use ticket stages: metadata attempt→reservation→transfer attempt→exactone nonnull bytes/memoryview result checked→decode attempt→validated.1000 sticky attempts apply ONLY to cell metadata SQL, conditional transfer SQL and decode, not scalar discovery/native-grant queries or allDBwork. Source/permission/discovery exceptions in admit_selected_owner_policy poison shared ledger even before first ticket. Failed load/codec/phase holds likewise poison; charges retained, no same-entry catch-and-retry or refunds. Context checks are not authorization.

Existing selected/source gate order remains: target reader and inherited-origin observer gates before any local/source cell load. Native resolve/currentness calls remain absent here. Exact conditional canonical BYTEA descriptors bind PK, identity, JSON type, size, SHA256 and cap in SQL BEFORE transfer. Transfer metadata is independently checked by fresh codec; no decoded cache. Each repeated load rechecks metadata and creates a new decoded object; byte/cell charges deduplicate only matching metadata but repeated work consumes attempts. Metadata view is read-only and contains no payload. RR alone is not protection against owntransaction writes; conditional SQL is required for that prehydration bound.

42 composed pure checks normal/-O pass (16 new adoption tests plus existing admission/codec/v1-ledger checks). Fake transport executes actual consumer phase sequencing and codec but never SQL or domain helpers. Coverage includes domain/local sharing, exact1MiB, attempts across phases/wrappers, conditional-row miss, malformed bytes/JSON, repeated-object mutation independence, metadata fingerprint conflict, context/principal change and pre-ticket discovery poisoning. Existing14 native definition source signatures/query observers adjusted for fresh actor and conditionalBYTEA; all remain UNRUN. DB-forbidden static/model/exact14 discovery passes. No actualSQL execution, native acceptance, fixture execution, migration, held/module inspection, backup change or activation.

Remaining: native PostgreSQL SHA256/conditionalSQL and ownwrite/concurrency proof; permission/source integration; scalargraph attempt composition; Finance/PMO adoption; full private template closure. Byte budget is not parsing-depth/RSS/CPU bound. Future additional domain integration must deliberately compose this ledger, not claim current separate ledgers already shared. Historical stage documents remain point-in-time source-only records.

Constructor/context failures in an active entry set a marker poison flag even before a ledger instance/ticket exists; a caught error cannot reset the operation by constructing a wrapper. Outside an entry the normal context denial remains. Generic load transport/decode errors become fixed ValidationError without copying details; native principal/source PermissionDenied and ValidationError from discovery remain native.
